## Reflection: PC Assemble Lab

### What I Learned
During the PC Assembly Lab, we attended a hands-on session in the laboratory where students
were divided into groups of five to six members. Each group was guided by a lab assistant
who explained the objectives and procedures of the activity. We were given a complete PC
and required to disassemble its components and then assemble it again correctly.
Through this activity, I learned how different hardware components such as the motherboard,
RAM, storage devices, and power supply work together in a computer system.

### Suggested Improvements
One improvement would be to provide more time for each group to explore the components
in detail and ask additional questions. This would help students gain a deeper understanding
of hardware troubleshooting and system configuration.

### Personal Reflection
Overall, this lab was very useful and practical. It helped me improve my confidence in
handling computer hardware and understand the importance of teamwork and careful handling
of components. The quiz at the end of the lab also helped reinforce what we learned during
the session.
